  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora's existing module framework needs revisiting. While the existing framework allows for some degree of extensibility by replacing existing modules, there's no easy way to add a completely new module without modifying server code (e.g. Server, DefaultManagement, or DefaultDOManager).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On April 16th, 2009, the committers discussed and agreed to move toward using Spring Dynamic Modules (OSGi) for Fedora's future module plugin framework.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Notes from whiteboard:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/download/attachments/11503659/modularity.jpg"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/download/attachments/11503659/modularity.jpg",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
