  "description": "<p>Fedora's existing module framework needs revisiting. While the existing framework allows for some degree of extensibility by replacing existing modules, there's no easy way to add a completely new module without modifying server code (e.g. Server, DefaultManagement, or DefaultDOManager).</p>\n\n<p>On April 16th, 2009, the committers discussed and agreed to move toward using Spring Dynamic Modules (OSGi) for Fedora's future module plugin framework.</p>\n\n<p>Notes from whiteboard:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/download/attachments/11503659/modularity.jpg\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/download/attachments/11503659/modularity.jpg</a></p>",
